 "summary": "Object Query Language standardised by the Object Data Management Group (ODMG-93, 2.0, 3.0): an SQL-like, functional and orthogonal query language over object databases with path navigation, nested collections, methods and struct/collection constructors. Derived from the O2 query language; subsets survive in Apache Geode and other object stores.",
 "status": "historical",
 "defined_by": [
  "consortium-standard"
 ],
 "standards": [
  "ODMG 3.0 (The Object Data Standard, 2000)"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://www.odbms.org/odmg-standard/",
 "influenced_by": [
  "sql"
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "The standard is the book 'The Object Data Standard: ODMG 3.0' (Morgan Kaufmann, 2000; not openly available). The ODMG disbanded in 2001; ODBMS.org hosts the remaining material.",
  "0": "No reference implementation survives in open source; Apache Geode implements an OQL dialect (ANTLR grammar oql.g)."
 },
